    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **291 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature so that when an owner is created, the response includes the count of other owners who already shared the same last name at that moment.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` `Integer namesakeCount` field with getter/setter. It's transient because the value is a snapshot computed at creation time, not persisted state (mirroring the intent, and avoiding a DB schema change).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Computes the namesake count *before* saving the new owner (so it counts only the *other*, pre-existing owners) via a new `countNamesakes(lastName)` helper that matches last names ignoring case. MapStruct maps the field into `OwnerDto` automatically by name.\n\n4. **Tests** \u2014 Added two integration tests: one verifying a novel last name reports `0`, and one verifying two existing (case-insensitive) namesakes yield a count of `2`, excluding the new owner itself.\n\nAll existing and new tests pass.",
